CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forwarding-reference pack forwards correctly: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Expanding a forwarding-reference parameter pack `A&&... a` in a call-argument
pattern `f(static_cast<A&&>(a)...)` now substitutes the type pack A in lockstep
with the value pack a (the k-th deduced element type), so perfect forwarding of
a pack -- the body of the variadic std::__invoke -- forwards correctly.
